<title>SINGAPORE: Eng Kong sets up repair service unit.</title>
<headline>Eng Kong sets up repair service unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Container service provider and depot operator Eng Kong Holdings said on Wednesday it has set up a specialised refrigerated container repair service unit with an initial investment of US$250,000.</p>
<p>It said in a statement US$500,000 working capital would be made available for NEK Reefer Services Ltd, which is expected to expand its repair services into Thailand, Malaysia and China.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that the potential growth from these markets will be at a much faster pace, thereby enhancing the group's operating margins,&quot; Eng Kong's executive chairman Eddie Li said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
